.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "JULY 2026" "Holberton School" "Simple Shell Man Page"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a command language interpreter that executes commands read from the 
standard input. It is a simplified implementation of a UNIX shell for 
educational purposes.
.PP
The shell displays a prompt and waits for the user to type a command.
Commands are executed using fork() and execve() system calls.
The shell searches the PATH environment variable to locate executables.
.SH INVOCATION
If no arguments are specified, simple_shell reads and executes commands 
from the standard input. A prompt is displayed after each command execution.
.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B env
Display all current environment variables in NAME=value format.
Returns 0 on success.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell and return to the parent process.
.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
When a command is entered, the shell performs the following steps:
.TP
1. Parse the command line into tokens
.TP
2. Check if command is a built-in (env, exit)
.TP
3. Search PATH for the executable using get_path()
.TP
4. Fork a child process using fork()
.TP
5. Execute the command using execve() in the child
.TP
6. Wait for the child process to complete using wait()
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B simple_shell
exits with one of the following values:
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 127
Command not found or execve() failed.
.TP
.B Other
Exit status of the command executed.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following examples show basic usage of simple_shell:
.PP
.B Example 1: List files
.TP
$ ./hsh
.TP
$ ls
.TP
file1.c  file2.c  shell.h
.PP
.B Example 2: Use absolute path
.TP
$ /bin/ls -l
.TP
-rw-r--r-- 1 user user 412 file1.c
.PP
.B Example 3: Print environment
.TP
$ env
.TP
USER=julien
.TP
HOME=/home/julien
.TP
PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:...
.PP
.B Example 4: Exit shell
.TP
$ exit
.SH FILES
.TP
.B main.c
Main shell loop and command routing
.TP
.B environ.c
Built-in env command implementation
.TP
.B exit.c
Built-in exit command implementation
.TP
.B exec.c
Process execution using fork(), execve(), and wait()
.TP
.B getline.c
User input reading functionality
.TP
.B token.c
Command line parsing and tokenization
.TP
.B path.c
PATH environment variable searching
.TP
.B shell.h
Header file containing function prototypes and includes
.SH SEE ALSO
.B sh(1), bash(1), execve(2), fork(2), wait(2), getenv(3)
.SH BUGS
The simple_shell does not support the following features:
.TP
- Pipes (|) and redirections (>, <, >>)
.TP
- Special characters (", ', `, \, *, &, #)
.TP
- Command history or tab completion
.TP
- Aliases or job control
.SH AUTHORS
Written by the Simple Shell development team.
See AUTHORS.md for a complete list of contributors.
.SH NOTES
This is a simplified shell implementation designed for educational purposes.
It is not intended as a replacement for standard UNIX shells such as sh or bash.
